# WS6-01/02 (toCString of a sub-view). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md §11 (toCString:
# `String` or `str` -> `cstring`, no allocation; the result is a loan of the argument)
# and spec/12-ffi-contracts.md / spec/appendix-stdlib.md ("`cstring` is a raw
# zero-terminated pointer"): the cstring of a `str` denotes exactly that str's bytes.
# The probe creates a file through toCString of the first 36 bytes of a longer path.
# Expected: the 36-byte name exists and the longer name does not. The runner removes
# build/tmp/assessment/WS6/f612-* before each run (54x-style clean start; see the
# falsifiability log), so a file from an earlier run cannot satisfy it.
# A rejection at compile time (slice of a `str` not accepted) is a spec-conformance
# finding against spec/appendix-stdlib.md §11 instead.
profiles: host hosted-amiga hosted-amiga-13
expect: output
contrast: slice(full, 0, 36) ==> slice(full, 0, 41)
contrast-expect: output
--- output
created true prefix true full false
--- contrast-output
created true prefix false full true
